Look in your $HOME directory... which will most likely (but not always) be
/home/%username%

You may need to do a "ls -a" in order to see the .nethackrc file because it
is a hidden file (as are all directories and files that begin with a "." in
Linux)

If there isn't one already in there, then you can just create a file there
with that name and insert the appropriate options. (check Chap. 9 of the
Guidebook for all of them, as I was so enthusiastically informed of not too
long ago...)

Hope this helps...

